        "exhibition": "the-work-of-the-surface",
        "slug": "modern/monolith-vigeland-granite",
        "text": "Intertwined bodies cover the column, with heads, backs and limbs emerging at different depths. Move around it to follow one figure into the next. Vigeland modeled the composition in 1924–1925; Ivar Broe, Nils Jønsson and Karl Kjær carved the granite from 1929 to 1942. This model records the column and its pedestal.",
        "priorCaptionsPreserved": 48,
        "priorWorkSlugsPreserved": 48,
        "coverAndOtherContentPreserved": true
      },
      {
        "exhibition": "bodies-in-motion",
        "slug": "modern/two-girls-back-to-back-vigeland-granite",
        "text": "Two crouching figures rest back to back and clasp their raised hands. Their bent legs spread the weight while the linked arms make another connection overhead. Turn the group to compare the faces and the spaces enclosed by their limbs. The provider identifies the granite sculpture as Vigeland’s Two Girls Back to Back; its exact date and site remain unconfirmed.",
